.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- scp with colon-path local names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I source
\&...
.I target
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
wraps
.BR scp (1)
with colon-path rewriting for local
.B BASE:LEAF
arguments (when
.I BASE
contains
.BR / ).
Forms like
.I host:path
(no slash before
.BR : )
are left unchanged for scp.
.PP
Destination directory placement follows the same
.I DEST/LEAF
rules as
.BR colon-cp (1)
for local destinations.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the rewritten
.B scp
command without executing it.
.PP
Other options are passed through to
.BR scp (1).
See the original manual for the complete option set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scp (1),
.BR colon-rsync (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
